.TH tucolumn n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tucolumn
.PP
\fBcolumn\fR\-like columnation in pure Tcl.
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tucolumn::table text  ?-separator S? ?-output S? ?-right 0|1?
::tclutils::tucolumn::fill  items ?-width N? ?-gap N?
::tclutils::tucolumn::text  text  ?...?           ;# alias for table
::tclutils::tucolumn::file  path  ?-mode table|fill? ?...?
.CE
.PP
Table mode aligns delimited columns (input separator defaults to whitespace runs; output separator defaults to two spaces). Fill mode arranges items column\-major into columns fitting \fB\-width\fR (default 80).
.SS Errors
.TS
l l.
Case	\fB\-errorcode\fR
\fBfile\fR: unknown \fB\-mode\fR	\fB{TCLUTILS TUCOLUMN MODE}\fR
\fBfile\fR: \fB\-mode\fR without value	\fB{TCLUTILS TUCOLUMN OPTION}\fR
unknown option	\fB{TCLUTILS COMMON OPTION \-name}\fR
\fB\-width\fR/\fB\-gap\fR not a positive integer	\fB{TCLUTILS COMMON INTEGER \-name}\fR
\fB\-right\fR not a boolean	\fB{TCLUTILS COMMON BOOLEAN \-right}\fR
.TE
.SS CLI
.CS
tclsh bin/tucolumn.tcl table file.txt
tclsh bin/tucolumn.tcl fill -width 60 words.txt
.CE
.SS "Line ends"
.PP
\fBtable\fR, \fBtext\fR and \fBfile \-mode table\fR return text that ends with LF exactly when the input does: \fB"b\enJörg\en"\fR gives a result with final LF, \fB"b\enJörg"\fR one without, like \fBtuhead\fR, \fBtutail\fR and \fBtunl\fR. Versions before 0.2 dropped the final LF.
